  quality-assurance.agent.md         <- agents/quality-assurance.md

How MavDitto uses them (src/content_writer/voice_method.py):

  * Selected sections are extracted by heading and inserted into the
    Content Writer's LLM prompts. Lines that only make sense inside Claude
    Code / Cowork (slash commands, `.claude/` paths, "delegate to the X
    agent", reference-file pointers) are dropped at load time.
  * The sales-oriented tone-by-context matrix and the before/after examples
    are NOT sent to the model: the examples illustrate the method with
    invented statistics for a fictional SaaS company, and this tool's
    guardrail forbids unsourced figures. MavDitto's own university
    tone-by-context matrix and examples live in config/brand-voice.json.

Nothing in this directory is edited in place; to change behavior, change
the extraction in voice_method.py or the brand profile in /config.
